# Plugging into the Transport Theorem (Finish the Problem)

Start from the transport theorem (acceleration form), expressed in the rotating \(B\)-frame:

\[
\mathbf a_B^{\,i}
=
\ddot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}
+
2\,\boldsymbol\omega\times\dot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}
+
\dot{\boldsymbol\omega}\times\mathbf r^{\,B}
+
\boldsymbol\omega\times(\boldsymbol\omega\times\mathbf r^{\,B})
\]

---

## Given (to plug in)

\[
\mathbf r^{\,B}=
\begin{bmatrix}
r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

So the \(B\)-frame derivatives are:

\[
\dot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}=
\begin{bmatrix}
\dot r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix},
\qquad
\ddot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}=
\begin{bmatrix}
\ddot r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Rotation about the \(z\)-axis:

\[
\boldsymbol\omega=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\dot\theta
\end{bmatrix},
\qquad
\dot{\boldsymbol\omega}=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\ddot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## Evaluate each term

### 1) Translational term \(\ddot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}\)

\[
\ddot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}=
\begin{bmatrix}
\ddot r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

### 2) Coriolis term \(2\,\boldsymbol\omega\times\dot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}\)

First compute:

\[
\boldsymbol\omega\times\dot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\dot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\times
\begin{bmatrix}
\dot r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
\dot\theta\,\dot r\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Multiply by \(2\):

\[
2\,\boldsymbol\omega\times\dot{\mathbf r}^{\,B}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
2\dot\theta\,\dot r\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

### 3) Euler term \(\dot{\boldsymbol\omega}\times\mathbf r^{\,B}\)

\[
\dot{\boldsymbol\omega}\times\mathbf r^{\,B}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\ddot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\times
\begin{bmatrix}
r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
r\ddot\theta\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

### 4) Centrifugal term \(\boldsymbol\omega\times(\boldsymbol\omega\times\mathbf r^{\,B})\)

First:

\[
\boldsymbol\omega\times\mathbf r^{\,B}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\dot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\times
\begin{bmatrix}
r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
r\dot\theta\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Then:

\[
\boldsymbol\omega\times(\boldsymbol\omega\times\mathbf r^{\,B})
=
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
0\\
\dot\theta
\end{bmatrix}
\times
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
r\dot\theta\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
-r\dot\theta^2\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

---

## Sum all terms

\[
\mathbf a_B^{\,i}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
\ddot r\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
+
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
2\dot\theta\,\dot r\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
+
\begin{bmatrix}
0\\
r\ddot\theta\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
+
\begin{bmatrix}
-r\dot\theta^2\\
0\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Combine components:

\[
\boxed{
\mathbf a_B^{\,i}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
\ddot r - r\dot\theta^2\\
r\ddot\theta + 2\dot r\,\dot\theta\\
0
\end{bmatrix}
}
\]